  bootwright / install
      Prepare this host's baseline packages and controller Python runtime from the locked
      wheels carried by this build. This command selects no context. Use --dry-run to show the
      planned changes, with the locked wheel inventory in JSON or YAML. Use --check to verify
      host readiness, including the packages, runtime, setup receipt and state root. Both flags
      use local reads only. A ready host needs no setup. When installation is needed, install
      shows dnf's own preview before confirmation. --yes skips ordinary confirmation during
      execution.

  Usage
    bootwright install [flags]

  Command flags
      --check    Verify the existing installation and exit 1 if it is not ready
      --dry-run  Show what install would change without running dnf
      --yes      Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright install --dry-run
